    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88373bda_f52dd241",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb_upgrade.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-19T23:36:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has been there since the very beginning of the USB update implementation.\n\nHow about we leave it here for backwards compatibility but just don\u0027t send this request from the server. (a modification for a separate patch).",
      "parentUuid": "db249f97_447123eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c7dd595f2abffddc9f6c2ca748e4206de1e27264",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db249f97_2418a78b",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb_upgrade.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 233,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-19T19:38:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But do we reset the state to idle? Doesn\u0027t look like it.\n\nI think we should be prepared for the update to be abandoned or restarted by the other end at any time (AP reboots, CCD goes away, someone hits ^C, whatever). We should expect to get back-to-back transfer start messages, or another start message instead of rebooting, or a short packet, or any other thing.\n\nA test for this would be nice, which would require moving this into common/.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 233,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c7dd595f2abffddc9f6c2ca748e4206de1e27264",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88373bda_55d13e27",
        "filename": "chip/g/usb_upgrade.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 233,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-19T23:36:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we actually have a timeout (checked in line 129) which resets the protocol state if there is no traffic for 5 seconds.\n\nI would rather modify this behavior in a different patch if still is necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "db249f97_2418a78b",
